# QMS software documentation (Neubond)

> **Scope note:** This rule is inherited from `Neubond-App-v2` and describes the Loop I device,
> firmware, and Flutter app QMS. Its paths (`docs/qms/`, `lib/`, `ios/`, `west.yml`) refer to those
> repositories, not this web app. Kept here for when the web app enters IEC 62304 scope.

When the user asks to **create**, **draft**, **write**, or **update** QMS / regulatory / DHF software documentation, follow this workflow.

**Product context:** **Neubond Loop I** — **Class I** medical device, **Class B** software (IEC 62304). Use *Neubond Loop I* / *Loop I* in regulated prose. Do **not** use internal codenames (gamma, gammaV1, ArmIO, nubizBoard, board targets) in QMS text.

## 1. Read instructions and template

Read `docs/qms/instructions_for_qms_docs.md` in full — especially **Documentation scope**, **Document set and phases**, **How documents relate (traceability)**, **Writing rules**, and **Authoring workflow**.

Read the matching official template in **`docs/qms/Templates/`** when one exists (naming: `<DocCode>_template.md`, e.g. `SOUP_template.md`, `SRR_template.md`). Draft to the **controlled record** path under the phase folder, not the template file.

| Templates (structure only) | Controlled record |
| -------------------------- | ----------------- |
| `docs/qms/Templates/SOUP_template.md` | `docs/qms/Phase III/SOUP.md` (**NBD-LP1-SOUP-001**) |
| `docs/qms/Templates/SRR_template.md` | `docs/qms/Phase IV/SRR.md` (**NBD-LP1-SRR-001**) |
| `docs/qms/Templates/work_instruction_template.md` | eQMS / DHF (engineering drafts: `docs/qms/work_instructions/`) |

Do **not** treat `docs/qms/Templates/` files as approved controlled records.

## 2. Documentation scope (mandatory)

QMS artifacts describe the **entire Neubond Loop I software architecture**:

| Layer | In scope |
| ----- | -------- |
| **Wearable firmware** | Loop I wearable on nRF52840; Zephyr OS + nRF Connect SDK (NCS); BLE GATT; EMG, haptics, storage; OTA via MCUboot + MCUmgr/SMP |
| **Mobile app** | Production **iOS on iPad** — BLE, therapy/calibration/monitoring, OTA UI |
| **Backend** | Supabase, Next.js auth web, Vercel hosting, Resend email (see **NBD-LP1-SOUP-001** for top-level SOUP rows) |
| **Monitoring** | Sentry crash reporting on the production iOS app (**SOUP-04**) |

**Mobile app filter:** production **iOS only**. Exclude Android, USB serial, debug tools, internal test/research-only features, and non-production app variants.

**Firmware baseline:** **`neubond-firmware/`** — not `Neubond-App-v2/firmware/` (legacy DHF). Prefer `west.yml`, production source, and interface docs over stale `neubond-firmware/docs/sop/` prose.

**Production firmware filter:** document **production** overlay behavior. Exclude bench/HIL overlays (`no_sleep_dev`, `hil_orchestrator`) and USB CDC from production system narratives unless the user expands scope.

Cross-item interfaces: **BLE** (firmware and app), **HTTPS** (app and backend).

## 2b. Out of scope — `docs/sbom/` (mandatory)

`docs/sbom/` is **engineering workspace only** — outside the QMS boundary.

When executing any **create qms …** workflow:

- Do **not** read, write, edit, create, or delete anything under `docs/sbom/`.
- Do **not** run engineering SBOM generator scripts (`sbom_generate*.py`) as part of QMS work.
- Do **not** reference paths under `docs/sbom/` in QMS artifacts or in chat outputs for QMS tasks.
- Controlled SBOM records are **only** under `docs/qms/Phase III/`: **NBD-LP1-SBOM-001** (`SBOM.md`), `sbom_*.json`, `vulnerability_report_*.json`.
- If machine-readable SBOM files need regeneration, tell the user to run **generate sbom** / **generate sbom ios** separately. Update Phase III JSON only when the user supplies promoted artifacts or explicitly asks.

## 3. Identify phase and document type

| Phase | Documents | Controlled record paths (see instructions for full table) |
| ----- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| I — Planning | SDP; URS/IPS (**read-only**) | `docs/qms/Phase I/` |
| II — Inputs | SRS, HZC, SAD | `docs/qms/phase-ii-inputs/` |
| III — Outputs | SDD, SOUP, SBOM, CMP | `docs/qms/Phase III/`, `docs/qms/phase-iii-outputs/` |
| IV — Verification & release | CVR, test protocols, SRR | `docs/qms/phase-iv-verification/`, `docs/qms/Phase IV/SRR.md` |
| V — Validation | TBD | `docs/qms/phase-v-validation/` |

## 4. Read upstream docs first

Read `docs/qms/Phase I/IPS.md` and `docs/qms/Phase I/URS.md` before drafting Phase II+ artifacts. **Never edit IPS or URS** — immutable approved references.

Read upstream controlled records in the same or earlier phase. Align the document under edit. Do not contradict IPS or URS.

**Cross-document issues — report only.** Do not edit other QMS files unless the user explicitly requests it. End with **Cross-document impact** when other docs need changes.

## 5. Gather evidence (in-scope only)

| Layer | Sources |
| ----- | ------- |
| **App (iOS)** | `lib/` (exclude Android/USB/debug-only), `docs/app_guide/ble_communication.md`, `docs/app_guide/ota.md`, `docs/app_guide/sentry.md`, `docs/app_guide/ios_commands.md`, `pubspec.yaml`, `ios/Podfile.lock` |
| **Firmware** | **`neubond-firmware/`**: `west.yml`, `prj.conf`, `src/`, `overlays/production.conf`; `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/COMMUNICATION_DESIGN.md`, `docs/ios_ota_integration.md`, `docs/learn/51_gatt_design.md` |
| **Backend** | Supabase and backend auth usage in app and backend code, deployment/ops guides |

Do not use `usb_communication.md`, Android guides, or legacy `Neubond-App-v2/firmware/` as production QMS evidence.

## 6. Draft using Neubond conventions

Follow **Writing rules** in `instructions_for_qms_docs.md`. Key agent checks:

- **American English**; preserve IPS/URS wording when quoting.
- **Full, complete sentences** in body text and SOUP narratives.
- **Avoid semicolons** where separate sentences read clearer.
- Write **Section** (not the section symbol).
- **No arrows** in official QMS prose. Use *traces to*, *feeds*, *aligns with*, *implements*.
- **Controlled document IDs:** **`NBD-LP1-<DocCode>-001`** when citing QMS records (not `NBM-LP1-…`).
- Engineering guides (`docs/app_guide/`, `docs/ops_guide/`) are inputs — **not** controlled QMS records.

**Regulatory concepts (do not conflate):** SOUP risk register (**NBD-LP1-SOUP-001**), SBOM inventory (**NBD-LP1-SBOM-001**), supplier approval (separate procedure), CSV (not applicable to app development). Top-level System SOUP list and evaluation details live in **NBD-LP1-SOUP-001** and `docs/qms/Templates/SOUP_template.md` — do not invent or shorten the list in the rule file.

**Verification (Phase IV):**
- **Unit** = feature-level (aligns with SAD). Export/reformat automated tests where possible.
- **Integration** = component-to-component.
- **System** = end-to-end (BLE, therapy flows, cloud, auth).
- Not all tests need 1:1 SRS links. Backend/SOUP-dependent behavior may trace via SOUP management plus integration/system tests.
- Cybersecurity controls verified in **NBD-LP1-CVR-001** per **NBD-LP1-CMP-001**.

## 7. Write output

Draft to the **controlled record** path in `instructions_for_qms_docs.md`. Follow the matching **`docs/qms/Templates/`** template for section structure. Remove template *Guidance* blocks and `«placeholders»` before approval.

Use `[TBD]` for missing controlled content. Do not invent user needs or hazards.

End with **Cross-document impact** if other docs need changes.

**draft only**: chat only. Do not commit unless asked.
